  "id": "Compound::DB01075 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Diphenhydramine is shown to bind to Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including limonene. The evidence suggests that Cyp2c9 participates in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, an enzyme that catalyzes the oxidation of limonene. This activity is then participated by Cyp2c19, indicating a potential functional relationship between these two enzymes. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and significant interaction, likely involving the enzymatic oxidation of limonene by Cyp2c19. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in the metabolism of limonene across different pathways supports the idea that Diphenhydramine may influence the activity of Cyp2c19 through its interaction with Cyp2c9. The mechanistic link is supported by the observed participation of Cyp2c9 in the same metabolic pathway, reinforcing the possibility that Diphenhydramine could modulate Cyp2c19 activity through this route.",
